  "verdict": "NOT SUPPORTED AT STRENGTH -- right-signed but weak, and the paradigm-ordering assumption is REFUTED. Within 22 real recordings the measured ratio is right-signed on localization error (Spearman rho = -0.36, p = 0.0991) -- Exp C's direction -- but it does not clear the pre-registered -0.40 bar and is not significant at this n. More decisively, the ordering the design assumed is false: MEASURED, sleep-onset (W->N1) is not a higher-ratio transition than eyes-open/closed alpha (median R 0.68 vs 0.69) and localizes no better (median e_norm 0.156 vs 0.078). So (i) the design did not actually span the ratio axis -- W->N1 is a gradual, low-ratio transition on this geometry -- and (ii) Exp C's synthetic 'robust across paradigm strength' (15/15 at every ratio) does NOT transfer: real localization degrades badly at low ratio and is not rescued at the nominal 'high-ratio' paradigm, the same synthetic-overstates-real pattern already documented for Exp A. This is the pre-registration's negative branch (ordering violated); it is reported as such, and the fair test -- a genuinely high-ratio real transition (e.g. N2<->REM) as the high end -- is registered as a follow-up rather than run post-hoc to chase the bar.",
